# Packages removed from the base image. build.sh removes these one at a time and
# tolerates a miss, so a package that upstream already dropped is reported by
# catspaw-verify rather than failing the build.
#
# Measured against the booted image before writing: nearly every GNOME app this
# was meant to strip (gnome-tour, maps, weather, contacts, totem, rhythmbox,
# cheese, simple-scan, boxes, calendar, clocks...) is ALREADY absent. Bazzite
# removes them upstream. Only yelp survives, so this list is short on purpose.

# --- GNOME leftovers
yelp

# --- Gaming Mode session
# The gamescope *session* is the Big Picture / Gaming Mode shell. Removing it
# leaves the desktop session alone and is the point of a Hyprland-first image.
gamescope-session-steam
gamescope-session-plus

# --- OOBE
bazzite-portal

# --- Steam Deck cosmetics
steamdeck-backgrounds
steamdeck-gnome-presets

# ===========================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT REMOVED -- do not add these without understanding the cost:
#
#   gamescope, gamescope-libs, gamescope-shaders
#       The compositor binary itself, separate from the session. Still useful
#       in desktop mode for per-game scaling and frame limiting via
#       `gamescope %command%` in a Steam launch option.
#
#   jupiter-fan-control      Steam Deck FAN CONTROL. Removing this is a
#                            thermal problem, not a debloat.
#   jupiter-hw-support-btrfs Deck hardware quirks and firmware support.
#   steamdeck-dsp            The speaker DSP profile. Without it the built-in
#                            speakers sound wrong.
#
#   steam / steam-devices    Removing Steam from a Steam Deck is not debloating.
# ===========================================================================
